<resources>

  <!--
    The system splash screen, which exists from API 31.

    Left alone, the platform draws the launcher icon here - and draws it on a 288dp canvas, against the 108dp that an adaptive icon foreground is authored at.
    Upstream's foreground was a vector and scaled to any size for nothing; this fork's is a render, so that 2.67x is a real upscale and the icon arrives soft.
    ic_splash_icon is the same artwork authored at the size the splash actually draws, which is the whole fix: 288dp canvas, artwork inside the centred 192dp circle, per the platform's own icon spec.

    The background is set rather than inherited so the splash matches the first frame the app paints.
    It follows values/values-night like every other colour here, though the system resolves it from the device's dark-mode setting rather than from the theme the user picked inside the app - a splash is drawn before there is an app to ask.
  -->
  <style name="AppTheme.Splash" parent="AppTheme">
    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/themeBackground</item>
    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/ic_splash_icon</item>
  </style>

</resources>
